OL,3,GNEWSAWorker left unable to communicate
OL,4,Aafter load fell
OL,5,
OL,6,FA company has been fined #4m after a
OL,7,Fworker suffered life-changing brain and
OL,8,Fspinal injuries that left him unable to
OL,9,Fcommunicate and now living in a care
OL,10,Fhome with round-the-clock care.
OL,12,FThe 40-year-old, from Telford, was
OL,13,Fcrushed by a 231kg (36 stone) forklift
OL,14,Fload while working at City Electrical
OL,15,FFactors Limited's Proteus Switchgear
OL,16,Fdivision in Stafford Park in October
OL,17,F2024.
OL,19,FThe Health and Safety Executive (HSE)
OL,20,Fsaid the load fell from a forklift
OL,21,Ftruck while heavy equipment was being
OL,22,Floaded onto a lorry.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
